{
  "_comment": [
    "Template for .mcp.json — copy to .mcp.json and replace the <...> placeholders.",
    "The real file is gitignored because every path below is machine-specific.",
    "",
    "KICAD_MCP_PROFILE and KICAD_MCP_OPERATING_MODE are two independent axes:",
    "the profile decides which tools exist (agent_full = 391, build = 24), the",
    "operating mode decides whether they may write. Setting only one of them is",
    "the most common way to end up without any schematic tools.",
    "",
    "KICAD_MCP_KICAD_CLI is only needed when kicad-cli does not come from the",
    "system package — e.g. when KiCad runs as a Flatpak. In that case create a",
    "wrapper and point this at it:",
    "",
    "  #!/bin/sh",
    "  exec flatpak run --command=kicad-cli org.kicad.KiCad \"$@\"",
    "",
    "Without it the server talks to one KiCad release over IPC while running",
    "every export, ERC and DRC through another. Check with kicad_get_version():",
    "the reported CLI version and IPC version must match.",
    "",
    "The IPC socket needs no configuration — the KiCad Python API finds both the",
    "native and the Flatpak socket on its own, and KiCad 10 enables its API",
    "server by default. Note that a Flatpak KiCad only sees $HOME, /media and",
    "/run/media, so project files must not live under /tmp."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "openscad": {
      "command": "uv",
      "args": [
        "run",
        "--with",
        "git+https://github.com/quellant/openscad-mcp.git",
        "openscad-mcp"
      ]
    },
    "kicad": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": [
        "kicad-mcp-pro"
      ],
      "env": {
        "KICAD_MCP_PROJECT_DIR": "<absolute path to this repository>",
        "KICAD_MCP_PROFILE": "agent_full",
        "KICAD_MCP_OPERATING_MODE": "write",
        "KICAD_MCP_KICAD_CLI": "<absolute path to kicad-cli, omit if the system one is correct>"
      }
    }
  }
}
